  ["BTh"] = "Não problem.",
  ["BTi"] = "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 Ouro?",
  ["BTj"] = "[PT] Here you are. Take care.",
  ["BTk"] = "Sorry, you don't have eNãough money.",
  ["BTl"] = "[PT] Beds, chairs, tables, statues and everything you could imagine for decorating your home!",
  ["BTm"] = "[PT] I have {beds}, {chairs}, {containers}, {decoration}, {flowers}, {instruments}, {pillows}, {pottery}, {statues}, {tapestries} and {tables}. Which of those would you like to see?",
  ["BTn"] = "[PT] Beds, chairs, tables, statues and everything you could imagine for decorating your home!",
  ["BTo"] = "[PT] In this category I have '{Bruise Bane}', '{Cure Bleeding}', '{Wound Cleansing}', \\z\n\t\t'{Cure Poison}', '{Intense Wound Cleansing}', '{Recovery}' and '{Intense Recovery}'.",
  ["BTp"] = "[PT] In this category I have '{Light}', '{Find Person}', '{Magic Rope}', '{Levitate}', '{Haste}', \\z\n\t\t'{Charge}' and '{Great Light}'.",
  ["BTq"] = "[PT] I can teach you {healing spells}, {attack spells} and {support spells}. \\z\n\t\tWhat kind of spell do you wish to learn? \\z\n\t\t\tYou can also tell me for which level you would like to learn a spell, if you prefer that.",
  ["BTr"] = "[PT] <sigh> lost... word...",
  ["BTs"] = "[PT] <sigh> ohhhh.... memories...",
  ["BTt"] = "[PT] The secrets... too many... sleep...",
  ["BTu"] = "[PT] Loneliness...",
  ["BTv"] = "[PT] ..what about {magic}..",
  ["BTw"] = "[PT] <sigh> lost... word...",
  ["BTx"] = "[PT] <sigh> ohhhh.... memories...",
  ["BTy"] = "[PT] The secrets... too many... sleep...",
  ["BTz"] = "[PT] Loneliness...",
  ["BU"] = "I am 486486 and NãoT 'Blinky' as some people called me ... before they died.",
  ["BU0"] = "[PT] There are many books in the {academy}. Theory can be just as important as practice.",
  ["BU1"] = "[PT] It's my duty to protect this village and its {citizens}.",
  ["BU2"] = "[PT] It looks like you have mastered the drill.",
  ["BU3"] = "Sorry, I don't Comércio. Ask the shop owners for a Comércio instead.",
  ["BU4"] = "I don't approve of her opening a bar. Those drunken adventurers stumbling over the bridge at nighttime are Nãot especially Ajudaful in improving the situation.",
  ["BU5"] = "[PT] Such a chicken-hearted person.",
  ["BU6"] = "He Venders {weapons}. His shop is south west of town, close to the {temple}.",
  ["BU7"] = "[PT] He dedicated his life to welcoming newcomers to this island.",
  ["BU8"] = "[PT] She has her own problems.",
  ["BU9"] = "[PT] There's something about this guy I don't like.",
  ["BUA"] = "[PT] I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  ["BUB"] = "[PT] I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  ["BUC"] = "[PT] Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  ["BUD"] = "[PT] You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  ["BUE"] = "The druids Nãorth of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  ["BUF"] = "[PT] You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  ["BUG"] = "[PT] The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  ["BUH"] = "[PT] Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  ["BUI"] = "[PT] Keep your adventurer's stone well.",
  ["BUJ"] = "[PT] Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for free?",
  ["BUK"] = "[PT] Here you are. Take care.",
  ["BUL"] = "Não problem.",
  ["BUM"] = "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 Ouro?",
  ["BUN"] = "[PT] Here you are. Take care.",
  ["BUO"] = "Sorry, you don't have eNãough money.",
  ["BUP"] = "Bye, |JogadorNAME|.",
  ["BUQ"] = "Greetings, |JogadorNAME|! You're looking really bad. Let me heal your wounds.",
  ["BUR"] = "<Nãods> At your service, |JogadorNAME|, protecting the {village} from {Monstros}.",
  ["BUS"] = "Are you injured or poisoned? I can Ajuda you.",
  ["BUT"] = "[PT] Zerbrus, at your service.",
  ["BUU"] = "[PT] I'm the guard of this bridge. I defend Rookgaard against the beasts of the {wilderness} and the {dungeons}, and even of the stinking {sewers}.",
  ["BUV"] = "My duty is eternal. Time is of Não importance.",
  ["BUW"] = "Before you fight Monstros, deposit your money there. If you die, you won't lose it if it's save in the bank.",
  ["BUX"] = "[PT] Fine.",
  ["BUY"] = "I have to stay here, sorry. But I can {heal} you if you are wounded. I have also valuable information about {Monstros}.",
  ["BUZ"] = "I'm an expert concerning the wildlife and {Monstros} on this island.",
  ["BUa"] = "I'm Nãot a gossiper, but if you want to kNãow something about a certain Rookgaardian, ask.",
  ["BUb"] = "They're Nãot that dangerous, but don't let yourself get cornered by many of them. They still can hurt.",
  ["BUc"] = "There are two types of spiders on this island: Nãormal spiders and poison spiders. As their name says, the latter ones can poison you which will cause a constant loss of your health. Beware of them!",
  ["BUd"] = "[PT] For Rookgaard! For Tibia!",
  ["BUe"] = "[PT] Once you have upgraded your starter {equipment} a little - maybe leather stuff - and got a better weapon as well as a shield, you should be able to kill trolls.",
  ["BUf"] = "[PT] You need a stronger weapon than the starter club to kill wolves. Maybe a {sabre} or a short {sword} will do.",
  ["BUg"] = "[PT] The orcs have a hideout under the troll cave, just descend deep. Still, be very careful!",
  ["BUh"] = "MiNãotaurs are very strong. You will need a group of people or at least level 6 and good equipment to be able to kill them.",
  ["BUi"] = "They are a little tougher than they look like, but they're still good beginner Monstros.",
  ["BUj"] = "[PT] The skeletons on this island are usually fairly hidden. They are often found near graves and always underground. Beware of their evil life drain.",
  ["BUk"] = "[PT] There is a bear cave close to this bridge. Be careful, though, they hit hard!",
  ["BUl"] = "Wasp hives exist only behind the Nãorth bridge, so ask {Dallheim} for information. I'm glad there are Não wasps here. They always make me jump.",
  ["BUm"] = "Snakes can poison you, too, but their poison is usually Nãot as dangerous as that of poison spiders. Just be careful and kill them fast.",
  ["BUn"] = "[PT] Premium warriors pay. They gain many advantages this way.",
  ["BUo"] = "Não Monstro shall go past me.",
  ["BUp"] = "[PT] HAIL TO THE KING!",
  ["BUq"] = "It's Nãorth of the temple.",
  ["BUr"] = "A place of protection. Nãothing can harm you there.",
  ["BUs"] = "I can mark you some dungeons on your map if you ask me about {Monstros} suited for your level.",
  ["BUt"] = "[PT] The sewers are crowded with {rats}. They make fine targets for young heroes.",
  ["BUu"] = "[PT] There are {wolves}, {bears}, {snakes}, {deer}, and {spiders} in the wilderness past this bridge.",
  ["BUv"] = "I'm a follower of {BaNãor}.",
  ["BUw"] = "[PT] The heavenly warrior! Read {books} to learn about him.",
  ["BUx"] = "You will learn about magic soon eNãough.",
  ["BUy"] = "[PT] In the world of Tibia, many challenges await the brave adventurer.",
  ["BUz"] = "[PT] The premium side of Rookgaard lies beyond.",
  ["BV"] = "It's 1, Nãot 'Tibia', silly.",
  ["BV0"] = "[PT] I wait. I wait for someone like you to come here. I wait for them to grow disconsolate. I wait for them to despair. And I wait for them to die. Muhahaha.",
  ["BV1"] = "[PT] I am Zumtah, Zumtah the impeccable, Zumtah the marvellous, Zumtah the... the... eternal.",
  ["BV2"] = "[PT] The land you are currently dwelling in, human. Don't you have any sense of your surroundings?",
  ["BV3"] = "I have seen many of them. I have seen many of them die. In here, with me. Perhaps you will be pleased to meet them. Nãot long and you will join their ranks. Muhaha.",
  ["BV4"] = "[PT] Pesky creatures. Many of them have been brought here, many of them died here. Humans, lizards, beasts, they all die the same. Down here, with me. Muhahaha.",
  ["BV5"] = "[PT] What? What do you mean by that?",
  ["BV6"] = "Hmm, an old one. I don't care much about politics or power, as here, he has Nãone. Here, only I have power. Muhaha.",
  ["BV7"] = "What are you talking about, such things do Nãot matter down here. Down here alone, isolated and broken. Muhaha.",
  ["BV8"] = "[PT] If you purchase premium time for your account, this opens up a lot of possibilities. ...",
  ["BV9"] = "[PT] For example, you will be able to travel off the mainland, ride a mount and benefit from offline training as well as having more outfits and magic spells to choose from.",
  ["BVA"] = "Want to kNãow what Monstros are good for you at your level? Just ask me!",
  ["BVB"] = "She's very attractive. Too bad my duty leaves me Não time to date her.",
  ["BVC"] = "[PT] He guards the temple and can heal you if you are badly injured or poisoned, just like me.",
  ["BVD"] = "[PT] She's {Obi's} granddaughter and deals with {armors} and {shields}. Her shop is south west of town, close to the temple.",
  ["BVE"] = "[PT] One of these reclusive druids.",
  ["BVF"] = "Her shop is just Nãorth of the bridge. She really has good offers.",
  ["BVG"] = "[PT] Gentle girl, but a little to esoteric for my taste. However, her {potions} might come in handy.",
  ["BVH"] = "[PT] You can find the oracle on the top floor of the {academy}, just above {Seymour}. Go there when you are level 8.",
  ["BVI"] = "[PT] The local {bank} clerk.",
  ["BVJ"] = "[PT] His job of teaching young heroes is important for the survival of all of us.",
  ["BVK"] = "He's the local tanner. You could try Vendering fresh corpses or leather to him.",
  ["BVL"] = "Greetings, |JogadorNAME|! You're looking really bad. Let me heal your wounds.",
  ["BVM"] = "He does a fine job, protecting the Nãorth bridge. He's been on duty longer than me and kNãows the Nãorth side of Rookgaard well.",
  ["BVN"] = "[PT] At your service.",
  ["BVO"] = "He's a farmer. A little more friendly than his cousin {Willie}, he also Comprars and Venders {food}.",
  ["BVP"] = "He's quite rude. Also, he Comprars and Venders {food}.",
  ["BVQ"] = "You are poisoned. I will Ajuda you.",
  ["BVR"] = "[PT] You are looking really bad. Let me heal your wounds.",
  ["BVS"] = "[PT] You aren't looking really bad. Eat some food to regain strength.",
  ["BVT"] = "<Nãods> At your service, |JogadorNAME|, protecting the {village} from {Monstros}.",
  ["BVU"] = "Bye, |JogadorNAME|.",
  ["BVV"] = "Hmm, |JogadorNAME|. I really don't kNãow if you should go into the wilderness without a shield. You should earn some money by hunting rats under the village first until you can afford at least a wooden shield.",
  ["BVW"] = "Are you injured or poisoned? I can Ajuda you.",
  ["BVX"] = "[PT] For Rookgaard! For Tibia!",
  ["BVY"] = "Não Monstro shall go past me.",
  ["BVZ"] = "[PT] The premium side of Rookgaard lies beyond.",
  ["BVa"] = "Want to kNãow what Monstros are good for you at your level? Just ask me!",
  ["BVb"] = "[PT] Come over here if you have to resupply!",
  ["BVc"] = "I wish someone could spare a minute and Ajuda me...",
  ["BVd"] = "[PT] This is too hard for an old woman like me.",
  ["BVe"] = "Olá, young adventurer, you look strong eNãough to Ajuda me!",
  ["BVf"] = "[PT] Feel the wind in your hair during one of my carpet rides!",
  ["BVg"] = "[PT] I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  ["BVh"] = "[PT] I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  ["BVi"] = "[PT] I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  ["BVj"] = "[PT] Never heard about a place like this.",
  ["BVk"] = "[PT] Do you seek a passage to ",
  ["BVl"] = "[PT] We would like to serve you some time.",
  ["BVm"] = "[PT] I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  ["BVn"] = "[PT] I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  ["BVo"] = "[PT] I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  ["BVp"] = "[PT] I can fly you to {Darashia}, {Edron}, {Issavi}, {Svargrond}, {Kazordoon}, {Zao} or to {Femor Hills} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  ["BVq"] = "[PT] I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  ["BVr"] = "[PT] Feel the wind in your hair during one of my carpet rides!",
  ["BVs"] = "[PT] Don't forget to deposit your money here in the Global Bank before you head out for adventure.",
  ["BVt"] = "Bah, I kNãow. I received some sort of 'Nãomination' from our outpost in Port Hope. ...",
  ["BVu"] = "Usually it takes a little more than that for an award though. However, I hoNãour Myra's word. ...",
  ["BVv"] = "I hereby grant you the right to wear a special sign of hoNãour, ackNãowledged by the academy of Edron. Since you are a woman, I guess you don't want manly stuff. There you go.",
  ["BVw"] = "Bah, I kNãow. I received some sort of 'Nãomination' from our outpost in Port Hope. ...",
  ["BVx"] = "Usually it takes a little more than that for an award though. However, I hoNãour Myra's word. ...",
  ["BVy"] = "I hereby grant you the right to wear a special sign of hoNãour, ackNãowledged by the academy of Edron. Since you are a woman, I guess you don't want manly stuff. There you go.",
  ["BVz"] = "I Vender equipment for your adventure! Just ask me for a {Comércio} to see my wares.",
  ["BW"] = "[PT] Uglyness incarnate. One eye! Imagine that! Horrible!",
  ["BW0"] = "In this state we can serve the Great Snake in a more suitable way. You have to understand that it is an hoNãour and a privilege, Nãot a sacrifice.",
  ["BW1"] = "[PT] The attacks of the enemy forces are fierce but we hold our ground. ... ",
  ["BW2"] = "[PT] I'd love to face one of their generals in combat but as their masters they cowardly hide far behind enemy lines and I have other duties to fulfil. ... ",
  ["BW3"] = "I envy you for the chance to thrust into the heart of the enemy, locking weapons with their jaws... or whatever... and see the fear in their eSim when they recognise they were bested.",
  ["BW4"] = "I have Não idea what kind of creeps are behind all this. Even the gNãomes don't and they have handled that stuff way more often. ...",
  ["BW5"] = "But even if we knew Nãothing more about them, the fact alone that they employ the Ajuda of those mockeries of all things dwarfish, marks them as an enemy of the dwarves and it's our obligation to annihilate them.",
  ["BW6"] = "[PT] Ships are a comfortable way of travelling to distant cities. At any harbour, you can board the ship and ask its captain where he sails to.",
  ["BW7"] = "Travelling by ship will cost you some Ouro, though, so be sure to have money with you.",
  ["BW8"] = "[PT] Aye, Tibia is a vast world, my friend, with plenty of adventures, harbours, and loot! \\z\n\t\t\tThe Mainland is open to everyone; but there are many beautiful islands and more cities to explore, \\z\n\t\t\tif you have premium rights and can use a ship.",
  ["BW9"] = "[PT] Once you have reached level 8 here on this isle, you can choose your definite vocation and leave for the Mainland.",
  ["BWA"] = "[PT] In a just world, I would be captain of a grand ship, ...",
  ["BWB"] = "Those pirates out there would Nãow be my minions, and we would brave the seas and become the terror of the coastal towns! ...",
  ["BWC"] = "[PT] If only our plan had worked!",
  ["BWD"] = "Captain Kid sold his ship to Comprar pointless things like those insanely expensive locks for the cell doors. ...",
  ["BWE"] = "He said the caNãoes would do for a while. ...",
  ["BWF"] = "I got the impression he was Nãot overly sad to part with the ship because he was kNãown to suffer a lot from seasickness.",
  ["BWG"] = "[PT] I'd have been a much better captain then Kid was. I played several captains on stage and I was good! ...",
  ["BWH"] = "[PT] Where Kid longed for the appreciation of his men, I would rule by fear and with an iron fist!",
  ["BWI"] = "It was all captain Kid's idea. You see, he hated his name and planned to become kNãown by the name captain Kidnap. ...",
  ["BWJ"] = "[PT] All he needed was someone famous to kidnap. ...",
  ["BWK"] = "[PT] Given his men's dismal lack of talent and intelligence that would have been quite a feat. ...",
  ["BWL"] = "[PT] We knew each other from a few scams we did together in the past, so he contacted me. ...",
  ["BWM"] = "I was to impersonate the famous Princess Lumelia. You kNãow, the one everyone was looking for. ...",
  ["BWN"] = "[PT] That would show his men and the other pirates what a great kidnapper he was. ...",
  ["BWO"] = "[PT] He promised me that I would become his second in command and lead a wonderful life of plundering, robbing and pillaging. ...",
  ["BWP"] = "[PT] So I agreed to impersonate the Princess for a while and it worked fine at first. ...",
  ["BWQ"] = "[PT] He returned with me dressed as the Princess from a raid on his own and was instantaneously the hero of the day for his men. ...",
  ["BWR"] = "[PT] Things went bad when they decided to have a victory party. ...",
  ["BWS"] = "[PT] As far as I could make out from the mumblings of the pirates, Kid lost the key to my cell while relieving himself in the underground river. ...",
  ["BWT"] = "[PT] The fool decided to dive after it .. never to be seen again. ...",
  ["BWU"] = "[PT] When I found out about Kid's demise I tried to convince the pirates it was a hoax, but they just won't believe me!",
  ["BWV"] = "Ah kidnapping is so much fun. That is, if you're Nãot on the receiving end. ...",
  ["BWW"] = "[PT] It's easy money and you have a chance to frighten and torture someone who can't fight back!",
  ["BWX"] = "[PT] The more stupid the people are, the easier it is to con them. ...",
  ["BWY"] = "[PT] And the poorer they are the less means they have to get revenge. Har Har! ...",
  ["BWZ"] = "[PT] So I make sure I ruin those I scam. Then they have other things to worry about than getting revenge on me.",
  ["BWa"] = "The key was lost in the underground river and has probably washed into the seven seas by Nãow! ...",
  ["BWb"] = "If that stupid Kid hadn't been so obsessed with kidnapping he'd Nãot have sold his ship to Comprar the most expensive and complicated locks for his cells!",
  ["BWc"] = "[PT] As long as we stick to undefended coastal towns we can make an easy fortune. Har Har! ...",
  ["BWd"] = "[PT] As soon as I get out of here I'll finally become a pirate captain on my own. I don't need Captain Kid!",
  ["BWe"] = "Those fellows Ajuda still green adventurers like you, so you learn the lay of the Tibian Mainlands. \\z\n\t\tWith the adventurer's stone you can reach their guild hall from all major temples. ...",
  ["BWf"] = "[PT] I recommend you travel there as soon as possible.",
  ["BWg"] = "Leading the charge! It's a war down here. I maintain the outer defences and supplies which are organised back in Kazordoon and also by the gNãomes. ...",
  ["BWh"] = "I have sealed some of the areas far too dangerous for anyone to enter. If you can prove you're capable, you'll get an oportunity to Ajuda destroying the weird machines, pumping lava into the caves leading to the most dangerous enemies.",
  ["BWi"] = "But even if we knew Nãothing more about them, the fact alone that they employ the Ajuda of those mockeries of all things dwarfish, marks them as an enemy of the dwarves and it's our obligation to annihilate them.",
  ["BWj"] = "The CGB is a patriotic organisation that fights our numerous enemies with means that guards or army do Nãot have at their disposal. ...",
  ["BWk"] = "[PT] We work secretly and covertly. We uncover secret plots and we are both the first line of defence of our city and the last. We are joined only by the best of the best.",
  ["BWl"] = "[PT] The AVIN is rather a crime syndicate than anything else. If there is something dirty and illegal, they are most likely involved. ...",
  ["BWm"] = "They are unscrupulous and also do Nãot back away from blackmailing and assassination.",
  ["BWn"] = "[PT] The TBI is as old-fashioned, stubborn and inflexible as only males can be. What makes this bureaucracy somewhat dangerous, is the money they have at their disposal. ...",
  ["BWo"] = "They Comprar spies and traitors - all of them weak-willed or greedy individuals.",
  ["BWp"] = "[PT] The elves of Ab'Dendriel are our allies. Our druids contribute most to keeping such a good relation. ...",
  ["BWq"] = "[PT] They seem to understand the elves a bit better than we ordinary people do.",
  ["BWr"] = "The name of the city is a cruel joke. The people there are oppressed by Thais and VeNãore who slowly bleed the isle and its people white. ...",
  ["BWs"] = "[PT] It shows what would have happened to us if our rebellion had failed.",
  ["BWt"] = "We have located twelve graves that have to be secured: In the old Nãorthern Edron graveyard, in the dark cathedral of the plains of havoc, in the ghostlands, on Cormaya, Somewhere in the Femor Hills, on Vengoth, ...",
  ["BWu"] = "in the graveyard of Darashia, in the old temple Nãorth of Thais, at the entrance to the orcland, one is on the southern ice islands, in a mountain on Kilmaresh, one on an island Nãorth-east of Ankrahmun.",
  ["BWv"] = "[PT] The Great Snake deserves that we try to use the best of our abilities and capabilities to serve it. Our existence is a test in this world corrupted by the egg stealers. ...",
  ["BWw"] = "[PT] Only when we overcome all obstacles cast into our way, we will become worthy to serve the Great Snake in all eternity.",
  ["BWx"] = "Some of the relics are still left in this world. They are insignia of the snake god's power. We kNãow that you came for one of those insignia. ...",
  ["BWy"] = "The Great Snake approves that you acquire its holy sceptre. We will Nãot Missãoion the wisdom of the god to hand this relic to one of the false-born.",
  ["BWz"] = "[PT] We were once the heigh priests of the Great Snake. We willingly left our mortal existence behind to become bound to this temple. ...",
  ["BX"] = "[PT] 485611800364197.",
  ["BX0"] = "[PT] The fae vary greatly in size and appearance. There are different kinds of fae like fauns, pixies, pookas, swan maidens, nymphs and boogies. Those mystical creatures are wielding power in magic and elementals. ...",
  ["BX1"] = "[PT] Most of them are rather reclusive and live peaceful lives in their secret realm. Sometimes they are called the ,children of dreams' or ,the dream born' because the fae are born from the mortals' dreams.",
  ["BX2"] = "[PT] It doesn't seem that the cults share a common theme or object of reverence but there has to be some connection beyond being at the centre of culminations of disruptive power from beyond. ...",
  ["BX3"] = "The connection is of second thought though. Connected or Nãot, they further the death of our world. That alone makes it imperative to dig those cults out and destroy their cores. ...",
  ["BX4"] = "[PT] We won't be able to rout our each and any movement but if we manage to neutralize the worst, we gain some time and deny the enemy much of its leverage on the future of our world.",
  ["BX5"] = "[PT] We have located some of the worst culminations of otherworldly presence and our sources returned information about them with different results of success. ...",
  ["BX6"] = "[PT] Some information I can provide you will be rather sparse and much is left to speculation but you should have at least some lead where to go and investigate.",
  ["BX7"] = "[PT] We haven't completely figured out what our enemy exactly is. For one, this thing defies all laws of nature and comprehension, ...",
  ["BX8"] = "that understanding it is either impossible or twist a mind in ways that are Nãot meant to be. Also the Yalahari who figured out way too much about the thing, became tainted and changed by this kNãowledge ...",
  ["BX9"] = "And ultimately Nãot only fell and became his, they also provided the thing with something of their own, be it kNãowledge, understanding or even direction, purpose. ...",
  ["BXA"] = "[PT] Precisely ",
  ["BXB"] = "[PT] , young one.",
  ["BXC"] = "Sim, I remember him well. It was a tragedy. An earthquake led to a cave-in and many of our brave miners died. ...",
  ["BXD"] = "[PT] Their ghosts still haunt the Grothmok tunnel in which they died, so we had to seal it off.",
  ["BXE"] = "This place became a fiery trap to certain beings with an affinity to fire. Somehow it reconnects randomly with the kNãown world, to which it once belonged ...",
  ["BXF"] = "[PT] but also to other places that it shares some affinity with like hellish places of unspeakable evil that spawn infernal creatures.",
  ["BXG"] = "We kNãow about other planes of existence but in all history it has never been as easy to reach them as it is Nãow. ...",
  ["BXH"] = "Sometimes world seem to overlap and we can identify more and more such planes and worlds. More then we ever had imagined. All we can tell is, that something is changing. And Nãot for the good.",
  ["BXI"] = "GNãomish supplies and ingenuity have Ajudaed to establish and fortify this outpost. ...",
  ["BXJ"] = "Our kNãowledge of the enemy and it's tactics would be of more use if the dwarves would listen to us somewhat more. But gNãomes have learned to live with the imperfection of the other races.",
  ["BXK"] = "[PT] Our surveys of the area showed us some spikes in heat and seismic activity at very specific places. ...",
  ["BXL"] = "We conclude this is Não coincidence and the enemy is using devices to pump up the lava to flood the area. We have seen it before and had to retreat each time. ...",
  ["BXM"] = "[PT] This time though we might have a counter prepared - given me manage to pierce their defences.",
  ["BXN"] = "[PT] Some call us nature spirits or peri but we prefer the term fae. Most of us are rather reclusive and live peaceful lives in our secret realm. We only leave it in order to protect our home. ...",
  ["BXO"] = "[PT] We tend to be secretive about our true nature, but I guess there was once an elven sage who visited our realm and put his experiences down on paper. There might be a book about the fae in the library of Ab'Dendriel.",
  ["BXP"] = "[PT] I'll tell you something. I have seen such a creature once, far on the ice to the east. It was the coldest winter I can remember and the chakoyas were roaming the ice almost everywhere. ...",
  ["BXQ"] = "[PT] To evade them, me and the boys had to walk a long way to a spot where the ice was treacherous and thin. ...",
  ["BXR"] = "And there I've seen such a creature. The boys went almost mad and I turned my sled immediately. Não idea how we made it home. True story.",
  ["BXS"] = "[PT] The quara are the curse of the sea. Everybody that dares to enrage the sea spirits has to fear their vengeance. They come at night to kidnap people who forgot their lucky charms at home ...",
  ["BXT"] = "[PT] Sometimes those evil beings take the most naughty children to raise them as their own underwater.",
  ["BXU"] = "[PT] I'm a member of a circle of persons, that joined wisdom and resources for a common purpose. Let's say, we have an eye on the greater picture in the matters of our world. ...",
  ["BXV"] = "We are watching and evaluating what is happening in our world.\tTrying to avert the worst and offering a Ajudaing hand where we deem it needed. ...",
  ["BXW"] = "We usually avoid to interfere directly in the affairs of the world and vain politics are Nãot our concern at all.",
  ["BXX"] = "[PT] Well, while I focus more on the matters of life, some of my peers have different approaches and emphasize other aspects of the world more in their observations. ...",
  ["BXY"] = "[PT] Regardless we share a common goal of balance and harmony.",
  ["BXZ"] = "Even we kNãow the individual that was somewhat of our funder, only as the wise man. ...",
  ["BXa"] = "[PT] He was the first to bring bright and dedicated minds together, to bring at least a little order and guidance into troubled and chaotic times. ...",
  ["BXb"] = "The order predates mankind and never bothered to give itself a name. Such assumptions of pretence and vanity have Não place in our mindset.",
  ["BXc"] = "Most times we are silent watchers and keeper of kNãowledge that share what they have learned with each other. We are more concerned about kNãowledge and wisdom and power means little to us. ...",
  ["BXd"] = "[PT] To solve problems we usually try to convince the right people to do the right thing. We usually even lack the means for a more direct interference.",
  ["BXe"] = "[PT] Sometimes it's necessary to do something about a situation that became threatening to the world itself. ...",
  ["BXf"] = "It is gladly a rare occurrence and usually it is sufficient to somewhat offer a guiding hand to avert a course that would lead to more dire consequences. Nãonetheless sometimes we have to interfere.",
  ["BXg"] = "[PT] The fae vary greatly in size and appearance. There are different kinds of fae like fauns, pixies, pookas, swan maidens, nymphs and boogies. Those mystical creatures are wielding power in magic and elementals. ...",
  ["BXh"] = "[PT] Most of them are rather reclusive and live peaceful lives in their secret realm. Sometimes they are called the 'children of dreams' or 'the dream born' because the fae are born from the mortals' dreams.",
  ["BXi"] = "[PT] Fauns are half-human, half-beast nature spirits inhabiting the woods and mountains of Feyrist. They are a slightly roguish but cheerful folk, lovers of wine and dancing. ...",
  ["BXj"] = "[PT] Fauns show a youthful and graceful aspect but they are also brave and fearless when it comes to defend themselves. As Maelyrra told me, they emerge from mortals' dreams about celebrations, music and dancing. ...",
  ["BXk"] = "[PT] Lately, some fauns on Feyrist are tainted by the mysterious, sinister force that is threatening Feyrist as well as the rest of Tibia.",
  ["BXl"] = "[PT] Pixies are small nature spirits and mythical creatures inhabiting the forests and plains of Feyrist. They are generally benign, but at times, they may also display mischievous traits. ...",
  ["BXm"] = "[PT] Like most of the fae, pixies love dancing and are often gathering in larger groups to dance on secluded glades. Pixies love flowers, butterflies, shimmering beetles, gems and other colourful things. ...",
  ["BXn"] = "[PT] They also love the taste of honey, sweetened oat and ripe grapes. As Maelyrra told me, pixies emerge from mortals' dreams about friends and family.",
  ["BXo"] = "[PT] Pookas are nature spirits in animal form, looking like big hares with a faintly glittering fur. They are benign but mischievous, for sure with good reason regarded as the tricksters among the fae. ...",
  ["BXp"] = "Pookas love to play pranks on others, snitching and hiding things or telling made-up stories. They are capricious and fickle creatures. Pookas emerge from mortals' dreams about gems, treasures and Ouro. ...",
  ["BXq"] = "[PT] Lately, some pookas on Feyrist are tainted by a mysterious, sinister force that is threatening Feyrist as well as the rest of Tibia.",
  ["BXr"] = "[PT] Swan maidens are fae who can shapeshift from human form to swan form. The magical item allowing this transformation is a swan feather cloak, a garment with swan feathers attached. ...",
  ["BXs"] = "[PT] Here on Feyrist it is always hard to tell whether a swan swimming on a lake is an ordinary animal or a swan maiden in her bird shape. ...",
  ["BXt"] = "[PT] They protect the wilds of their secret realm from every intruder and live in small flocks along secluded lakeshores. As Maelyrra told me, swan maidens emerge from mortals' dreams about flying.",
  ["BXu"] = "Nymphs are female nature spirits and usually take the form of beautiful, young maidens who love to dance and sing. They dwell in the hills and forests of Feyrist, often near lakes and streams and they can't die of old age Nãor illness. ...",
  ["BXv"] = "[PT] They have a special, strong bond to the plants and animals of their domain and are very protective of Feyrist's flora and fauna. As Maelyrra told me, nymphs emerge from mortals' dreams about love.",
  ["BXw"] = "[PT] Boogies are a rather twisted kind of fae. Other than pixies, nymphs or fauns they favour underground caves and tunnels over forests or lush meadows. ...",
  ["BXx"] = "Only at night, they are roaming the surface, chasing other fae and visitors to Feyrist alike. They were once clumsy yet peaceful fae, but they are Nãow twisted and tainted by a mysterious, sinister force.",
  ["BXy"] = "[PT] She's the queen of a fae court. You can find her on a glade in the deep forest. It was queen Maelyrra who granted me permission to stay here in Feyrist. ...",
  ["BXz"] = "[PT] I promised to inform her about anything I find out about the abominable force that threatens this world.",
